  "preamble": "Deaffrication of the aspirated alveolar affricate [tsʰ] to the aspirated stop [tʰ]. Taishanese, the Siyi Yue variety of Taishan in Guangdong, reads words with the Middle Chinese 清 initial (tsh in Baxter's transcription, reconstructed /t͡sʰ/) with [tʰ]: 七 'seven' MC tshit > Taishanese /tʰit̚⁵⁵/ and 草 'grass' MC tshawX > /tʰau⁵⁵/, where Guangzhou Cantonese keeps the affricate (cat1, cou2) and Yangjiang Yue has cat3 for 七. Wikipedia's Taishanese consonant table still lists /t͡sʰ/, so the outcome described here is that of the 清 initial, not of every aspirated affricate in the language.",
